// Round 3 L. `as "rt_alloc"` (or `as "main"`) names a symbol the runtime or
// the generated program defines itself; the extern then binds to the
// runtime's static function or the program's own main, not to a C library
// symbol. Names the generated C reserves should be rejected.
// error: name|reserved|clash
extern "c" fn f(n: int): ptr as "rt_alloc"
fn main() {}
